cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ScientificDiscoveryLab — a computational research laboratory with a preregistered, self-auditing instrument pipeline"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it and read AUDIT/DO_NOT_CLAIM.md. No physics discovery is claimed."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  A computational research laboratory spanning percolation physics, optical
  propagation, prime gaps, Feigenbaum constants, pseudorandom-number
  certification, water-sound response, and AI-consciousness measurement
  methodology. Built to a preregistered standard: claim layering, mandatory
  controls, adversarial falsification, evidence grading, append-only
  registries, and fail-closed runners. Its most substantive result is negative
  and methodological — a self-audit in which four defects were found in the
  laboratory's own instruments, one of which had previously been counted as a
  pass, and in which two of them made the laboratory's own anomaly look smaller
  than it really was. No physics discovery is claimed.
authors:
  - name: "ScientificDiscoveryLab contributors"
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - preregistration
  - falsification
  - audit
  - percolation
  - computational-physics
  - optics
  - pseudorandom-number-generation
  - numerical-methods
  - open-science
